## nat-rec-k-lie

The schematic version of the code looks like

```lean
/-- Lie: Nat.rec is K-like -/
def g (n : Nat) : Prop := Nat.rec True (fun _ _ => False) n

theorem k1 : ∀ n, g n := fun _ => trivial

theorem bad : False := k1 1
```

Not representable as a `leanfile`, since a module that overwrites `Nat.rec` cannot be
re-imported by the exporter. Generated by exporting

```lean
import Lean
open Lean Elab Command

noncomputable def g (n : Nat) : Prop := Nat.rec True (fun _ _ => False) n

run_meta do
  withOptions (debug.skipKernelTC.set · true) do
    addDecl <| .thmDecl {
      name := `k1, levelParams := []
      type := .forallE `n (mkConst ``Nat) (mkApp (mkConst ``g) (.bvar 0)) .default
      value := .lam `n (mkConst ``Nat) (mkConst ``True.intro) .default }
  addDecl <| .thmDecl {
    name := `bad, levelParams := []
    type := mkConst ``False
    value := mkApp (mkConst `k1) (mkRawNatLit 1) }
```

and flipping `"k"` on `Nat.rec`.

